      "writtenOn": "2023-04-13T08:31:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you specify how you\u0027re supposed to use this ?\n\nIn particular I am a bit concerned that when this is called, mTimestampSinceLastUpdateStats is not reset, which means we\u0027ll upload stats dating from the last update and that might be arbitrarily far in the past ; the time that wasn\u0027t recorded will instead be recorded in the next update. So for example, suppose you collect metrics at midnight every day :\n• start a keepalive at 00:00 immediately after collecting\n• keep it started the whole day\n• next collection will still have lifetime 0 and active lifetime 0\n• Then at 02:00 stop the keepalive\n• next collection will have 26h of lifetime\n\nThis doesn\u0027t sound like what we want, which to me means that you must update the lifetime at the same time you reset the stats. If that\u0027s true, there is likely a way you can guarantee that statically (e.g. return a snapshot as you reset).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "009276402a9b220d973465c6aeccfabc45da85b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
