      "writtenOn": "2023-04-13T08:31:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This ends up being relatively expensive (especially as you create one here and an identical one in l.269, and likewise in other methods)\n\nYou could exploit the fact that the network ID is a 16-bit int and the slot will never be over 256, so you could make an int out of these and use a SparseIntArray. Then you\u0027d have a helper method to make the int out of the 2 values. If you do that please comment carefully because it\u0027s not necessarily super obvious that it will always fit.\n\nAnother option is to have a SparseIntArray indexed only by the netId, containing arrays. You can do that because the number of hardware slots is known at boot time and can\u0027t change.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 259,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 259,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "009276402a9b220d973465c6aeccfabc45da85b2",
